# Git Secrets Patterns
# Patterns to detect potential secrets in code

# API Keys
.*[Aa][Pp][Ii][_-]?[Kk][Ee][Yy].*=.*['\"][A-Za-z0-9_\-]{20,}['\"]
.*[Ss][Ee][Cc][Rr][Ee][Tt].*=.*['\"][A-Za-z0-9_\-]{20,}['\"]
.*[Tt][Oo][Kk][Ee][Nn].*=.*['\"][A-Za-z0-9_\-]{20,}['\"]

# AWS
AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
aws[_-]?secret[_-]?access[_-]?key

# OpenAI
sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{48}

# Stripe
sk_live_[0-9a-zA-Z]{24,}
pk_live_[0-9a-zA-Z]{24,}

# GitHub
ghp_[0-9a-zA-Z]{36}
gho_[0-9a-zA-Z]{36}
ghs_[0-9a-zA-Z]{36}

# Generic Base64 encoded secrets (minimum 40 chars)
['\"][A-Za-z0-9+/]{40,}={0,2}['\"]

# Private keys
-----BEGIN (RSA|EC|OPENSSH|DSA|PRIVATE) PRIVATE KEY-----